      "story_id": 1,
      "headline": "Trump-Meloni diplomatic rupture over Pope Leo XIV defense and Sigonella base refusal",
      "summary": "A major falling-out between US President Trump and Italian PM Meloni erupted after Meloni called Trump's attacks on Pope Leo XIV 'unacceptable' following the pope's opposition to the Iran war. Trump retaliated with a Corriere della Sera interview calling Meloni 'shocking' and lacking courage, then escalated by citing Italy's refusal to allow US bombers to use Sigonella base, threatening that the US 'will not be there' for Italy. The rift dominated Italian and international coverage through the week, with opposition parties across the spectrum rallying behind Meloni and Foreign Minister Tajani defending her while managing alliance optics.",
